{
  "__comment": "NVisionX Backup Status — ALL EKS CLIENTS, ONE DASHBOARD. Same pattern as scan-activity-all-clients.json: top row = combined status across every selected client, below = one collapsible row per client with PostgreSQL + OpenSearch backup detail. Unlike the scan dashboard, this needs NO new exporter/metric - kube-state-metrics already exposes kube_job_status_*/kube_cronjob_* for every CronJob-spawned Job in every EKS cluster, so there's no mimir series-limit risk from adding brand-new series here. CronJob names (confirmed from nx-application-helm/charts/databases/templates/{postgresqlBackup,opensearchBackup}-cronjob.yaml): '<release>-postgres-backup' and '<release>-opensearch-backup', both in the 'default' namespace on every EKS client. Job status queries wrap in max() per client to avoid over-counting when successfulJobsHistoryLimit/failedJobsHistoryLimit retain more than one completed Job object at a time (each retained Job carries its own kube_job_status_succeeded=1 series). NOT YET VERIFIED LIVE - built by pattern-matching the existing single-cluster 'NX Database Backups' dashboard (uid nx-database-backups) rather than confirmed against real data. Check the combined-overview tiles first after import, same way the scan dashboard needed 3 iterations to get the cross-datasource sum transform right (reduce[reduceFields,sum] -> merge -> calculateField[reduceRow,sum] is the proven-working chain, reused here).",
